gomodel:6ab067da00011565
        a                      owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment           "Human counterpart of mouse model gomodel:6ab067da00011397, same structure. Facts resting on mouse data from PMID:35263589 are ISS (GO_REF:0000024) with the mouse gene; where the mouse model used ISS from a human ortholog, this model cites that human experimental evidence directly. Microglial and neuronal context is ISS from mouse." , "Curated with GO AI HUB. Human counterpart of gomodel:6ab067da00011397: REG3G-EXTL3 signalling suppresses the kynurenine pathway and protects HK1-dependent glycolysis." , "XIAP is modelled with signaling adaptor activity (GO:0035591), transferred by ISS from mouse Xiap. The underlying mouse data (PMID:35263589 Fig. 6C binding, Fig. 6D knockdown) do not establish which function XIAP performs; XIAP's established MF is E3 ubiquitin ligase activity, untested in this pathway." , "Quinolinate (CHEBI:29959) is not the direct product of any activity in this model. HAAO outputs cis,cis-2-amino-3-carboxymuconate 6-semialdehyde (CHEBI:77612, RHEA:17953), which cyclises to quinolinate spontaneously. There is no enzyme and therefore no activity unit for that step; the quinolinate node represents its product, and the HAAO -> SRC causal edge carries the biology." ;
        lego:conforms_to_gpad  false ;
        lego:modelstate        "production" ;
        dc:contributor         "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8769-177X" ;
        dc:date                "2026-10-26" ;
        dc:title               "REG3G-EXTL3 signalling suppresses the kynurenine pathway and protects HK1-dependent glycolysis (Human)" ;
        pav:providedBy         "http://geneontology.org" ;
        owl:versionIRI         gomodel:6ab067da00011565 ;
        biolink:in_taxon       obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

